# Pairs with SplitCompletes. Reproduces production before #4452 was fixed
# (#4466) as a liveness defect, with every fairness condition of the base left
# intact: an adaptive split may open its window while a resize is in flight,
# and once the flip moves the alias off the copy it is splitting, the split's
# coordinator steps are never enabled again (each requires the tree to still
# resolve to the split's copy), so a split that started never finishes.
# Production abandons such a split (AbandonRetargetedSplitAsync, #4264), which
# this module has no action for. A second edit lets the stranded split count
# as quiescent, so the mutant cannot deadlock and stutters forever with the
# split unfinished: the liveness property is the only thing TLC can report.
MODULE: SplitCompletesSplitDuringResize
TARGET: SplitCompletes
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: an adaptive split opens during a resize and is stranded by the flip, so it never completes
PERTURBS: SplitBegin

--- FIND
SplitBegin ==
    /\ sp = "idle"
    /\ rs = "migrating" \/ rz \in {"idle", "purged", "undone"}
--- REPLACE
SplitBegin ==
    /\ sp = "idle"
\* MUTATION: no interlock with an in-flight resize.
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"}
--- REPLACE
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
\* MUTATION: a split the flip stranded counts as quiescent.
    /\ sp \in {"idle", "done"} \/ alias # spCopy
--- END
